    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "c. A description of how the vector attraction reduction requirements are met.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Interpretation of this descriptive retention requirement changes which sludge-management monitoring/recordkeeping obligations are in scope (B) and how missing descriptions are classified versus required evidence (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "d. A description of how the management practices listed above in Section II.3 are being met.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Cross-reference to Section II.3 management practices is ambiguous without that section; different readings change which practices trigger monitoring/recordkeeping duties (B) and whether absent records reflect no-duty, no-data, or unresolved states (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "e. The recommended agronomic loading rate from the references listed in Section II.3.c. above, as well as the actual agronomic loading rate shall be retained.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Recommended versus actual agronomic loading rates may function as numeric compliance benchmarks (A); retention is an explicit obligation (B); and whether only one rate, both rates, or referenced Section II.3.c. values are required affects missing-evidence classification when rates are undocumented (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "f. A description of how the site restrictions in 40 CFR Part 503.32(b)(5) are met for each site on which Class B bulk sewage sludge is applied.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Applicability hinges on whether sludge is Class B and site-specific; different readings change which sites trigger this recordkeeping duty (B) and whether absent site descriptions indicate conditional non-requirement or missing required evidence (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "\"I certify, under penalty of law, that the management practices in §503.14 have been met for each site on which bulk sewage sludge is applied. This determination has been made under my direction and supervision in accordance with the system designed to ensure that qualified personnel properly gather and evaluate the information used to determine that the management practices have been met. I am aware that there are significant penalties for false certification including fine and imprisonment.\"",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "This certification defines a site-specific compliance attestation tied to §503.14; whether it is required and satisfied changes monitoring/recordkeeping obligation status (B) and whether a missing or partial certification is documented no-data versus inadequate evidence (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "h. A certification statement that all applicable requirements (specifically listed) have been met, and that the permittee understands that there are significant penalties for false certification including fine and imprisonment. See 40 CFR 503.17(a)(4)(i)(B) or 40 CFR Part 503.17(a)(5)(i)(B) as applicable to the permittees sludge treatment activities.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Which requirements are 'specifically listed' and which 503.17 subdivision applies depend on sludge-treatment activity type; different interpretations change the set of applicable monitoring/certification duties (B) and how to treat absent certifications relative to conditional non-applicability (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "i. The permittee shall maintain information that describes future geographical areas where sludge may be land applied.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "This forward-looking maintenance duty may or may not be currently triggered; interpretation affects whether ongoing recordkeeping is required now (B) and whether missing information reflects no present duty or unresolved expected evidence (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "j. The permittee shall maintain information identifying site selection criteria regarding land application sites not identified at the time of permit application submission.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Applicability depends on whether future or unidentified sites exist; different readings change present monitoring/recordkeeping scope (B) and the semantics of absent site-selection records (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "k. The permittee shall maintain information regarding how future land application sites will be managed.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Whether this obligation is presently active for anticipated but unopened sites affects required monitoring/recordkeeping (B) and classification of missing future-site management information (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "The person who prepares bulk sewage sludge or a sewage sludge material shall develop the following information and shall retain the information indefinitely. If the permittee supplies the sludge to another person who land applies the sludge, the permittee shall notify the land applier of the requirements for recordkeeping found i n 40 CFR 503 .17 for persons who land apply.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Role split between preparer and permittee, indefinite retention, and third-party land-application notification change who owes which recordkeeping duties (B) and whether missing records belong to the permittee, land applier, or remain unresolved (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "a. The location, by either street address or latitude and longitude, of each site on which sludge is applied.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Site-identification method and the 'each site' scope affect which land-application events require retained records (B) and whether incomplete locational data constitutes acceptable evidence or a missing-evidence case (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "b. The number of hectares in each site on which bulk sludge is applied.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Hectare denominators are needed to normalize pollutant loadings against limits (A); retention is an explicit duty (B); absent hectare data changes whether pollutant comparisons and missing-record states can be resolved (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "c. The date and time sludge is applied to each site.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Application timing determines monitoring-period assignment for FY2025 (A), establishes when recordkeeping is required (B), and affects whether gaps reflect no application, conditional non-requirement, or missing evidence (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "d. The cumulative amount of each pollutant in kilograms/hectare listed in Table 2 applied to each site.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Table 2 pollutant loadings are direct numeric quantities for compliance comparison (A); cumulative per-site retention is a core recordkeeping obligation (B); interpretation of 'cumulative' and Table 2 scope changes missing-data semantics when reported results are absent (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "e. The total amount of sludge applied to each site in metric tons.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Total applied mass can bear on loading-rate and pollutant-limit calculations (A), is a retained monitoring record (B), and its absence versus zero-application periods affects missing-evidence classification (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "\"I certify, under penalty of law, that the requirements to obtain information in §503.12(e)(2) have been met for each site on which bulk sewage sludge is applied. This determination has been made under my direction and supervision in accordance with the system designed to ensure that qualified personnel properly gather and evaluate the information used to determine that the requirements to obtain information have been met. I am aware that there are significant penalties for false certification including fine and imprisonment.\"",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "This certification ties record completeness to §503.12(e)(2) for each application site; whether it is satisfied changes obligation status (B) and how to interpret absent site records relative to required information-gathering (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/part_iv.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 9, Section part_i",
      "exact_span": "g. A description of how the requirements to obtain information in §503.12(e)(2) are met.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "The descriptive 'how met' element is separate from raw data retention; interpretation affects which procedural recordkeeping/monitoring steps are obligatory (B) and whether missing narratives leave cases unresolved or document conditional non-requirement (C)."
    }
  ]
